::: {.doc-subject}

Validate that column values exist in a reference table (referential integrity).
:::

::: {.doc-usage-source}
Usage

[Source](https://github.com/posit-dev/pointblank/blob/main/pointblank/validate.py#L15351-L15533){target="_blank" rel="noopener"}
:::

::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}
```pythonsignature
Validate.col_vals_in_table(
    columns,
    ref_table,
    ref_column,
    na_pass=False,
    pre=None,
    thresholds=None,
    actions=None,
    brief=None,
    active=True,
    dimension=None,
)
```
:::

::: {.doc-text}

The `col_vals_in_table()` validation method checks whether each value (or composite key) in
the specified column(s) of this table exists in the corresponding column(s) of a reference
table. This is a referential integrity check: it catches orphaned foreign keys, broken
references, and values that fall outside a controlled vocabulary maintained in another
table.

Each row is a test unit. Rows whose key values are found in the reference table pass. Rows
with orphaned values fail. Failing rows are extractable via `get_data_extracts()` just like
any other column-level validation.

Cross-backend matching is supported: the reference table can be from a different backend
(e.g., a Polars DataFrame checked against a DuckDB table, or a MySQL table checked against a
SQLite table). The lighter table is automatically materialized to match the heavier table's
backend before comparison.
:::

## Parameters {.doc-parameters}

::: {.doc-definition-items}
<code>[columns]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [str | list[str]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>

:   The column (or list of columns for composite keys) in this table that should reference
    the other table. For composite keys, supply a list of column names.

<code>[ref_table]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Any]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>

:   The reference table containing the valid values. Can be a DataFrame, a database table,
    a file path (e.g., to a CSV or Parquet file), a database connection string (e.g.,
    `"duckdb:///path/to/db.ddb::table_name"`), or a callable that returns one of these. A
    path or connection string is loaded at interrogation time, as with
    [`tbl_match()`](`pointblank.Validate.tbl_match`); if the reference table can't be
    loaded, the step is marked as having an evaluation error.

<code>[ref_column]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [str | list[str]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>

:   The column (or list of columns for composite keys) in the reference table to check
    against. Must have the same length as ``columns``.

<code>[na_pass]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [bool]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[False]{.va}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   If `True`, rows where the key column(s) are null will pass. If `False` (default), null
    key values are treated as failing (not found in reference).

<code>[pre]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Callable | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   An optional preprocessing function to apply to the data table before validation.

<code>[thresholds]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [int | float | bool | tuple | dict | Thresholds | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   Failure-condition thresholds for this step (overrides global thresholds).

<code>[actions]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Actions | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   Actions to take when thresholds are exceeded.

<code>[brief]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [str | bool | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   A brief description for this validation step.

<code>[active]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [bool | Callable]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[True]{.va}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   Whether this step is active (can be a bool or callable returning bool).

<code>[dimension]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [str | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   The data quality dimension tag for this step.
:::

## Returns {.doc-returns}

::: {.doc-definition-items}
<code> [Validate]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>

:   The `Validate` object with this step added (for method chaining).
:::

## Examples {.doc-examples}



Check that every `customer_id` in orders exists in the customers table:

::: {#cca2f485 .cell execution_count=2}
``` {.python .cell-code}
import pointblank as pb
import polars as pl

customers = pl.DataFrame({"id": [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]})
orders = pl.DataFrame({
    "order_id": [101, 102, 103, 104],
    "customer_id": [1, 2, 3, 99],
})

validation = (
    pb.Validate(data=orders)
    .col_vals_in_table(
        columns="customer_id",
        ref_table=customers,
        ref_column="id",
    )
    .interrogate()
)

validation
```

